# phosphor/extern/ holds the vendored Luau runtime and valijson as committed
# source tarballs, extracted at configure time. No version is named here on
# purpose: the authoritative pins are PHOSPHORSCRIPTING_LUAU_VERSION and
# PHOSPHORFSLOADER_VALIJSON_VERSION, and a copy in this comment had already
# drifted (it said 0.723 while the tree shipped 0.737). Mark the tree vendored
# so GitHub Linguist excludes it from language statistics, and binary so the
# archives are never diffed or merged.
phosphor/extern/** linguist-vendored
phosphor/extern/*.tar.gz binary

# Qt Linguist catalogs, not TypeScript. Linguist goes by the extension and
# counts these as TS, which is the same misattribution the vendored rule above
# exists to correct.
plasmazones/translations/*.ts linguist-language=XML
